<description>
Recolor each black or blue connected component with the color of the marker that borders it most.

Input structure
- The grid contains black regions, blue line components, and isolated non-black/non-blue marker pixels.
- Marker pixels are controls; the black and blue cells are the regions to recolor.
Rule
- Label black and blue cells separately using 4-connectivity.
- For each labeled component, count side-adjacencies to every marker pixel.
- Recolor the component with the marker color having the largest shared side boundary; equal counts use row-major marker order.
- Leave the marker pixels unchanged.
Key insight
- The color assignment is local to each original-color component and is decided by shared edge contact with nearby markers.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "black and blue 4-connected components plus non-black/non-blue marker pixels",
  "transform": "recolor each black or blue component by the adjacent marker color with the largest shared edge boundary; break equal contact counts by row-major marker position; preserve marker pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 13x13 [observed, all examples identical]
  base_colors: black (0) and blue (1) fill entire grid except marker pixels
  blue_walls:
    role: 4-connected path/chain structures that partition the black background into regions
    components: 1-5, total 43-50 cells (25-30% of grid)
    topology: mostly degree-2 chains (78-95%), endpoints 2-10, branch points 0-2
  black_regions:
    count: 3-5 components via 4-connectivity
    size_range: 2-110 cells; one large exterior region + smaller interior pockets
  markers:
    count: 3-7 pixels total, 3-6 distinct colors from {2..9}
    duplicate: at most 1 color appears twice; rest are unique
    placement: each replaces a black cell; neighbors are only black and/or blue (never another marker)
  constraint: every black and blue 4-connected component must be side-adjacent to >=1 marker
  transform:
    recolor each black/blue component with the marker color having max shared-edge contact
    ties broken by row-major marker position (top-left wins)
    marker pixels preserved in output; output contains only marker colors

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction with validation
  steps:
    1. Start with 13x13 black grid
    2. Draw 1-5 blue (1) path/chain structures using random walks on the grid;
